<title>CANADA: Bombardier unit wins C$63 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Bombardier unit wins C$63 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>SAINT-BRUNO, Quebec 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bombardier Inc said on Tuesday its U.K.-based Prorail subsidiary was awarded a contract worth about C$63 million by Eversholt Leasing Ltd for the overhaul and refurbishment of 381 Mark 2 passenger coaches.</p>
<p>Montreal-based Bombardier said the contract is to be carried out over the next three years.</p>
<p>Eversholt Leasing is one of three rolling stock leasing companies set up in preparation for the privatization of British Rail. The 381 coaches being refurbished by Bombardier represent 10 percent of Eversholt's fleet.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau  (416) 941-8100</p>
</text>
